## Goal
Build the Watchlist feature. Users can save stocks to one of three 
statuses: watchlist, researching, invested. Everything persists in 
Supabase using the anonymous session cookie. No auth required.

## Scope — Do NOT go beyond this
- No analytics dashboard yet (Step 4)
- No Cohere AI yet (Step 5)
- No auth, no login, no user accounts — ever

## Do Not
- Break the existing stock search grid or stock detail page
- Use any HTTP library — native fetch only
- Expose any API key to the browser
- Commit broken or incomplete code
- Touch dev or main branch

---

## Task 1 — Watchlist API routes

Create app/api/watchlist/route.ts:
- GET: read session_id from query params, fetch all rows from watchlist
  where session_id matches, return ordered by created_at desc
  Use createClient directly:
  const supabase = createClient(
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!
  )
- POST: body is { ticker, company_name, logo_url, sector, status, session_id }
  Validate all required fields (ticker, company_name, status, session_id)
  Upsert into watchlist (unique on session_id + ticker) so saving the 
  same stock twice updates the status instead of duplicating.
  Return { ok: true, data } on success.
- Both methods use createClient directly with env vars — never import 
  from @/lib/supabase

Create app/api/watchlist/[ticker]/route.ts:
- DELETE: read session_id from query params, delete the row where
  ticker and session_id both match. Return { ok: true } on success.
- PATCH: body is { status, session_id }
  Update status for the matching ticker + session_id row.
  Valid status values: 'watchlist' | 'researching' | 'invested'
  Return { ok: true } on success.
- Both methods use createClient directly with env vars

